{{Quote|A precise hit will start a chain reaction which should destroy the station. ''Only'' a precise hit will set up a chain reaction. The shaft is ray-shielded, so you'll have to use proton torpedoes.|[[General]] [[Jan Dodonna]] briefs Rebel pilots on the attack on the Death Star|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
[[File:Protontorpedo.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Proton torpedoes were used by Luke Skywalker to destroy the first Death Star.]]
'''Proton torpedoes''' were a type of [[Missile|explosive ordnance]] used throughout [[the galaxy]], fired from [[Proton torpedo launcher|specialized launchers]].<ref name="SW EOSAOV (SE)">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles (second edition)]]''</ref> Upon impact with a target, the [[proton warhead]] would release clouds of high-velocity proton particles in a focused explosion.<ref name="Cross">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref><ref name="Complete Vehicles">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref>

==Description==
Proton torpedoes possessed an explosive [[Proton warhead|warhead]] which was fired from specialized launchers, that upon impact expelled clouds of high-velocity proton particles to devastating effect.<ref name="SW EOSAOV (SE)" /> were capable of incredible maneuverability, such as making a 90-degree turn within a turning circle of one meter.<ref>''[[TIE''
Fighter Owners' Workshop Manual]]''<nowiki/>''</ref> They could penetrate [[ray shield]]s but were stopped by [[particle shield]]s. High-yield proton torpedoes, likes those carried on [[Acclamator-class transgalactic military assault ship|''Acclamator''-class assault ships]], could be used to conduct [[Base Delta Zero]] bombardments.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" />

==History==
They were used by the [[Royal Naboo Security Forces]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]], in which [[Anakin Skywalker]] destroyed the [[Trade Federation]] [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|command ship]] with proton torpedoes.<ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref>

[[Standard decade|Decades]] later, proton torpedoes were used by TIE bombers to bomb a carrier stolen by the [[Spectres]]. Later, they were used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Battle of Yavin]]. After examining stolen [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], a [[planet]]-destroying battle station operated by the [[Galactic Empire]], the Alliance determined the Death Star would get destroyed if proton torpedoes were fired into the [[Thermal exhaust port|exhaust port]] which led down into the [[reactor]] core. [[Red Leader]] [[Commander]] [[Garven Dreis]] attempted to fire his torpedoes down the shaft, but instead the torpedoes missed the target, impacting on the surface. Using [[the Force]], Anakin’s son [[Jedi]] [[Lieutenant]] [[Luke Skywalker]] successfully destroyed the station and killed [[Governor]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] and most of the Empire’s best forces at his hands using proton torpedoes from [[Red Five (T-65B X-wing starfighter)|his]] [[T-65B X-wing starfighter|T-65B]] [[X-wing starfighter]] during the battle.<ref name="Episode IV" />

in [[4 ABY]], [[Wedge Antilles]] used proton torpedoes against the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]]'s power regulator in the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref>

Around 30 [[Standard year|years]] after the destruction of the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station]], the [[Resistance]] used miniaturized [[MG7-A proton torpedo]]es<ref name="Cross" /> during their bombing run on [[Starkiller Base]]'s [[thermal oscillator]].<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

